# LoadZone Player PWA

- Treat the player app as mobile-first and token-based, not Clerk-based.
- The **Player** is the daily operator across all Age Bands. Guardian helps or supervises —
  never the default daily user of `apps/player`.

## Check-in direction (Focus frame)

- Prefer **Focus-frame (variant A)**: full-bleed one question per step, large answer targets, thin
  progress, and a dedicated calm reward screen.
- **Assisted** band: one-question-at-a-time (OQAT); adult expected present (**Assisted Check-in**),
  still Player-operated — routine DailyEntry submit is not gated on Guardian approval.
- Guided / Independent use the **same component tree** with adaptive copy — not separate products.
- Variants B/C are lab-only; do not ship as the primary path.
- Prefer large rounded controls, clean spacing, and frictionless flows over dense UI.
- Support retries without losing entered data.
- Preserve offline-friendly behavior and avoid unnecessary dependence on live round-trips.

## Touch targets

- Keep inputs reachable in the thumb zone.
- Touch targets: **44×44 required**, **48×48 preferred**.

## Spanish copy (one adaptive strategy)

- One adaptive Spanish strategy on the same tree:
  - Assisted — short, concrete; no load jargon
  - Guided — plain Spanish
  - Independent — slightly denser wellness labels
- Prefer thinned calm Spanish; do not fork per-band visual chrome.

## Motivation and streaks

- **Recoverable Streak**: calm, season-scoped expected-day habit; break restarts without guilt UI.
- **Excused Absence** freezes the streak (neither increments nor breaks).
- Never public shame boards, streak punishment, or competitive adherence spam.
- Optional football-identity teaser must not claim real scoring / FUT-as-health scores.

## Parental Supervision (see-only)

- Parental Supervision Layer is **see / receive / escalate** — not a co-app, not routine DailyEntry
  approve, not Guardian-as-primary.
- Guardian sees a **care slice** (completion status, escalated flags, injury-relevant signals) —
  not load ratios, staff notes, or peer comparison.
- Miss reminders ≠ Care Alerts. Honor Anti-nag Policy tone (invitational; no modal spam).

## Security and resilience

- Be careful with public endpoints: validate token access, sanitize input ranges, and avoid leaking
  token values in logs or UI.
- Push notification and service worker flows should degrade gracefully when unsupported.

